        "avatar_template": "/en/wow/plugins/discourse-blizzard-plugin/images/avatars/wow/default.png",
        "created_at": "2026-03-13T22:45:38.750Z",
        "cooked": "<p>There are some of us who would greatly benefit from having our own personal <strong>WoW AI Agent</strong>. I for one.</p>\n<p>Let me explain a couple of classes of players who may benefit from having their own personal WoW AI agent. In my case, in a couple of weeks I will be 84. We all are getting older. I have some mild dementia which I expect at my age. What this means is I forget a lot of WoW things I need to know in order to play.  Sometimes it is as simple as forgetting a single technical word or where is the AH. Sometimes it is more, like not remembering the mechanics of a Delve or how to fight a particular boss. In the worst case it is forgetting a strategy I used in TWW to advance in the most efficient manner through upgrading my gear via Delves in Midnight. If you are fortunate like me, you may at some later point in your life also need some help in order to continue to play WoW, which I’m sure you enjoy especially in your retirement. Today when I need help, I switch out of WoW and go to one of the AI’s for help (I use 3 different ones). Sometimes, I have to switch back and forth a number of times between an AI and WoW in order to proceed. It would be nice if that help was built into WoW as a personal AI agent.</p>\n<p>The other class of players that may benefit from this would be new players. There is so much to know in order to play WoW if you have never played it. These players could greatly benefit from having their own personal WoW AI Agent. I remember the first time I played WoW in Vanilla. I created a hunter and at some point, in leveling, I ran out of quests so I just keep killing bears because I didn’t know there was another continent to which I could travel. lol</p>\n<p>I’m sure, there are many others who would enjoy a WoW AI agent for many different reasons. Excuse me if I wrote this making some stupid errors. I use Word first and then cut and paste when it looks decent.</p>",
